.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PCI_CONFIG 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pci_config_address ,
.Nm pci_read_config8 ,
.Nm pci_read_config16 ,
.Nm pci_read_config32 ,
.Nm pci_write_config8 ,
.Nm pci_write_config16 ,
.Nm pci_write_config32
.Nd access PCI configuration space
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In kern/pci.h
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn pci_config_address "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset"
.Ft uint8_t
.Fn pci_read_config8 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset"
.Ft uint16_t
.Fn pci_read_config16 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset"
.Ft uint32_t
.Fn pci_read_config32 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset"
.Ft void
.Fn pci_write_config8 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset" "uint8_t value"
.Ft void
.Fn pci_write_config16 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset" "uint16_t value"
.Ft void
.Fn pci_write_config32 "uint8_t bus" "uint8_t slot" "uint8_t func" "uint8_t offset" "uint32_t value"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn pci_config_address
function builds a type 1 PCI configuration-cycle address for the requested
bus, slot, function, and byte offset.
The offset is aligned down to a 32-bit boundary as required by the x86 PCI
configuration ports.
.Pp
The
.Fn pci_read_config8 ,
.Fn pci_read_config16 ,
and
.Fn pci_read_config32
functions read typed values from PCI configuration space.
Byte and word reads are reconstructed from the containing 32-bit port access,
and word reads that straddle a dword boundary are read from both adjacent
configuration words.
.Pp
The
.Fn pci_write_config8 ,
.Fn pci_write_config16 ,
and
.Fn pci_write_config32
functions update PCI configuration space.
Byte and word writes preserve neighboring bytes within the containing 32-bit
configuration word by performing read-modify-write cycles.
Word writes that begin at the final byte of a dword are split across adjacent
configuration words.
.Pp
Offsets beyond the first 256 bytes of conventional PCI configuration space are
not accessible through these functions and read as all-ones.
.Pp
On systems that do not implement PCI configuration mechanism #1, the read
functions also return all-ones and the write functions are ignored.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The typed read functions return the requested value.
Out-of-range bytes read as
.Dv 0xff ,
out-of-range words as
.Dv 0xffff ,
and out-of-range dwords as
.Dv 0xffffffff .
.Pp
The write functions return no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bus 9 ,
.Xr device 9 ,
.Xr driver 9
